<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/wildfire-smoke.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/wildfire-smoke-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/wildfire-smoke.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/insurance-appraisal-services/">Services</a></li><li aria-current="page">Wildfire &amp; Ash Claim Appraisal</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">Appraisal service</p><h1>Wildfire and Ash Claim Appraisal in Washington</h1><p class="lede">From the Carlton Complex in the Okanogan to the 2023 Gray and Oregon Road fires near Spokane, wildfire has become one of Washington’s defining property risks. These claims need careful valuation from day one.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-y" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line light" href="/talk-to-an-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>Peak season</dt><dd>July–October</dd></div><div><dt>Key regions</dt><dd>East slope &amp; Inland NW</dd></div><div><dt>Big issues</dt><dd>Limits, ash, rebuild cost</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>Wildfire in Washington</h2>
<p>Washington’s largest wildfires have mostly burned east of the Cascade crest, where hot, dry summers meet grass, sagebrush and pine forest. The 2014 Carlton Complex destroyed hundreds of homes in Okanogan County. On Labor Day 2020, the Babb Road Fire swept through the town of Malden in Whitman County. In August 2023, the Gray Fire near Medical Lake and the Oregon Road Fire north of Spokane destroyed hundreds of homes within days. The 2015 Sleepy Hollow Fire showed that fire can reach neighborhoods in Wenatchee too.</p>
<h2>Total losses: is the limit enough?</h2>
<p>When a home is destroyed, the first question is often whether Coverage A is high enough to rebuild. Construction costs, code requirements and post-fire demand for contractors can push the rebuild price above a limit set years earlier. Extended replacement cost endorsements can help. Our <a href="/free-claim-calculators/wildfire-total-loss-coverage-check/">wildfire total-loss coverage check</a> lets you test the numbers yourself.</p>
<h2>Partial losses and smoke</h2>
<p>Homes that survive a wildfire can still have serious damage: ash in attics and ducts, smoke odor in insulation, heat-damaged siding and windows, and landscaping lost. These claims are often underpaid because the house looks intact from the street.</p>
<ul>
<li>Professional cleaning of HVAC systems, attics and wall cavities.</li>
<li>Replacement of heat-damaged windows, vinyl siding and roof components.</li>
<li>Contents cleaning or replacement for soft goods and electronics.</li>
<li>Debris removal and hazardous material handling for total losses.</li>
<li>Additional living expenses during evacuation and repairs.</li>
</ul>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Underinsured or non-renewed?</b>Questions about whether an insurer properly set limits, cancelled or non-renewed a policy are regulatory or legal matters. The Washington Office of the Insurance Commissioner has consumer advocates who can help, and an attorney can advise on legal claims.</div>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Do I have to rebuild on the same lot to get full replacement cost?<svg class="ico chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Policies differ. Some let you rebuild elsewhere or buy a replacement home, sometimes with limits. Read the loss settlement section and ask the insurer to confirm in writing.</p></div></details><details><summary>What if my contents were all destroyed?<svg class="ico chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Some insurers will pay part of the contents limit without a full itemized inventory after a total loss. Ask the insurer what it allows and get the answer in writing.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is smoke damage from a fire miles away covered?<svg class="ico chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Smoke from a wildfire is generally a covered fire-related loss under most homeowner policies, subject to policy terms. The dispute is usually how much cleaning or replacement is needed.</p></div></details></div><h2>Related services</h2><div class="cards3 tight"><a class="pcard rv" href="/insurance-appraisal-services/snow-ice-freeze-appraisal/"><span class="pcard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/snow-house.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/snow-house-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/snow-house.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1100px) 50vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="pcard-body"><span class="pcard-k">Related service</span><h3 class="pcard-t">Snow, Ice Dam &amp; Freeze Appraisal</h3><span class="pcard-p">Roof collapse, ice dams, frozen pipes and ice-storm damage from Washington’s winter weather.</span><span class="pcard-more">Learn more <svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></span></a><a class="pcard rv" href="/insurance-appraisal-services/carrier-estimate-review/"><span class="pcard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/calculator-paperwork.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/calculator-paperwork-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/calculator-paperwork.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1100px) 50vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="pcard-body"><span class="pcard-k">Related service</span><h3 class="pcard-t">Carrier Estimate Review</h3><span class="pcard-p">A line-by-line review of the insurer’s estimate before you decide whether to supplement or demand appraisal.</span><span class="pcard-more">Learn more <svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></span></a><a class="pcard rv" href="/insurance-appraisal-services/neutral-umpire-services/"><span class="pcard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/paperwork-review.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/paperwork-review-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/paperwork-review.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1100px) 50vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="pcard-body"><span class="pcard-k">Related service</span><h3 class="pcard-t">Neutral Umpire Services</h3><span cla